<BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/></TAB><BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>Sand for Gypsum Sand Float Finish</TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  Aggregates for finish-coat plaster should be less than No. 16 sieve size. Larger sizes may be added for 
finish appearance purposes.  Select sieve number that will provide the desired texture.  Float texture is governed 
by maximum sieve sizes of sand. Sieve sizes of 20 to 30 provide a fine float finish and 16 to 20 provide a coarse 
finish.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<TXT><RID>ASTM C842</RID>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<ITM>Sand Gradation:  Percentage retained by weight (plus or minus 2 percent) on each sieve.</ITM><BRK/>
